course: dictionary
lesson: 115
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists them as numbered senses, and the context tells you which one to use. Adopt is a good example: it has four meanings, so you need the clues around it to choose the right one.
explain: «Isla always knew she was adopted; her mum and dad told her when she was tiny, with a picture book about a family.» Here adopt means to take a child into your family legally and raise them as your own. The words family and tiny are the clues.
explain: A class might adopt a new rule, which means it starts using that rule. Nothing about a child or a pet is in that sentence, so those meanings do not fit. Always ask: does this meaning fit the whole sentence?
explain: Adopt can also be a formal word for voting to accept a plan or law. When you meet a word you already know in a new sentence, stop and check which meaning fits before you decide.
fact: Adopt means to take a child into your family legally and raise them as your own.
fact: Adopt also means to take a pet home from a shelter to care for.
fact: Adopt can mean to start using a new idea, plan, method or way of behaving.
fact: In formal English, adopt can mean to vote to accept a plan or law.
fact: Adopted, adopts and adopting are different forms of the same verb.
exercise: «Some children are adopted: they join a family that did not give birth to them, and they are just as much part of it.» What does adopted mean here? | Moved to a new town for work | Sent away to live on their own | *Taken into a family legally and raised as their own | Given a new name at school
exercise: The council voted to adopt the new park rules. What does adopt mean here? | *To vote to accept a plan or law | To take a child into a family | To take a pet home from a shelter | To close the park for good
exercise: We went to the shelter to adopt a rabbit. What does adopt mean here? | *To take a pet home to care for | To leave a pet at the shelter | To count how many rabbits there are | To paint a picture of a rabbit
test: Dad said we will adopt a new way of cooking our dinner. What does adopt mean here? | To vote for a law | *To start using a new method | To take a child into the family | To buy a new oven
test: Which meaning of adopt is the most formal? | To take a child into a family | To start using a new idea | To take a pet home from a shelter | *To vote to accept a plan or law
exam: «Isla always knew she was adopted; her mum and dad told her when she was tiny.» Which meaning of adopt fits this sentence best? | To pick a pet from a shop | *To take a child into your family legally and raise them as your own | To send a child to a new school | To vote on a rule for the class
